{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, שִׁמְשַׁי","hw":"שִׁמְשַׁי","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">שִׁמְשַׁי</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m.</strong>;—always <span dir=\"rtl\">שׁ׳ סָֽפְרָא</span>: <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:8\" href=\"/Ezra.4.8\">Ezr 4:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:9\" href=\"/Ezra.4.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:17\" href=\"/Ezra.4.17\">17</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:23\" href=\"/Ezra.4.23\">23</a> <strong>(</strong>Andr<sup>M 86*</sup> conj. OIran. caritative <span dir=\"rtl\">ששמי</span>, conformed to <span dir=\"rtl\">שׁמשׁ</span>, cf. Scheft <sup>92</sup>, who, however, prefers OBaktr. <em>simēzhi</em> = <em>simaēzhi</em>, n.pr.<strong>)</strong>.","next":"BDB Aramaic, שֵׁן","prev":"BDB Aramaic, שְׁמַשׁ²"}